    <string name="backup_action_help_summary">WebDAV setup and backup guide</string>
    <string name="backup_help_cd">Help</string>
    <string name="backup_help_title">WebDAV backup help</string>
    <string name="backup_help_intro_title">Overview</string>
    <string name="backup_help_intro_body">This app supports cloud backup via the WebDAV protocol. Any WebDAV-compatible cloud works; Nutstore (Jianguoyun) is recommended (about 1 GB free traffic per month is usually enough). A backup includes your library, groups, progress, bookmarks, highlights, reading settings, profile, and book content.</string>
    <string name="backup_help_jianguoyun_title">Nutstore setup</string>
    <string name="backup_help_jianguoyun_body">1. Open https://www.jianguoyun.com/\n2. Sign up or sign in\n3. Open Account info from the top-right menu\n4. Go to Security\n5. Under third-party apps, add an app and create an app password\n6. Enter the server URL, account, and app password in Me → Backup &amp; restore\n7. Keep the default subdirectory (MarkdownReader) unless you need another\n8. Run a manual backup once to verify\n9. To restore, pick the backup file you want</string>
    <string name="backup_help_auto_title">Auto backup</string>
    <string name="backup_help_auto_body">• After WebDAV is configured, the app auto-backs up once a day when you exit (back-to-exit works; force-stopping from Recents may not)\n• Same-day backups with the same filename overwrite; different dates are kept\n• If “Also upload latest backup” is on, remote backup.zip is also overwritten for quick restore</string>
    <string name="backup_help_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="backup_help_tips_body">• First backup fails: create a MarkdownReader folder at the WebDAV root, then retry\n• Auth fails: use the app password, not your login password\n• After restore, restart the app so all settings apply\n• WebDAV credentials stay on this device and are not overwritten by a restore package</string>
